    "notes": "- This particular Canadian pressing has pressing plant ID \"Q\" etched in deadwax on both sides, but is without [a703109]'s signature \"Aℓ\" on any of the two sides.\n- Printed inner sleeve with a band image and lyrics.\n\n[url=https://www.discogs.com/release/1239084]Release 1239084[/url]: this version has pressing plant ID \"Q\" and [a703109]'s signature \"Aℓ\" in deadwax on both sides.\n\nA1 titled 'Down To The Waterline' on back cover vs. 'Down To The Water Line' on A-side label.\n\n[On back cover:]\nRecorded at Basing St. Studios, London, Feb. 1978.\nCover painting by Chuck Loyola at Hothouse.\nFor [a1011285].\nThank you Robert Allan.\n℗ 1978 Phonogram Ltd.\nManufactured and distributed by PolyGram Inc., 6000 Cote de Liesse, St. Laurent, Quebec H4T 1E3 - Made in Canada\n\n[On inner sleeve:]\nLyrics reprinted by kind permission of Straightjacket Songs / Rondor Music.\n\n[On labels:]\nAll songs pub. in UK by Straight Jacket Songs/Rondor Music\n℗ 1978 Phonogram Ltd.\nManufactured and distributed by Polydor Ltd. 6000 Cote de Liesse, St Laurent, Quebec H4T 1E3 - Made in Canada",
